{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 20, :comments ["<b>And let us see what will become of his dreams.</b> Rabbi Yitzchak said: this verse cries out to be interpreted. The holy spirit says so — they say 'let us kill him,' and Scripture concludes 'and let us see what will become of his dreams' — let us see whose word will stand, if yours or Mine. For it is impossible that they would say 'and let us see what will become of his dreams,' since once they kill him his dreams are nullified."], :book :genesis, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 37, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T09:02:25.913625523Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}